# Roc-native interfaces and Markdown-first documents

Rocci connects Roc's compile-time guarantees with ordinary HTML, CSS, and a small desktop host. This site is the working tree for public docs: add pages under `site/`, keep chrome in `site/theme/`, and preview with `rocdown run site`.

:card-grid.begin
    :link-card[page: "docs/start/what-is-rocci", title: "Getting started", summary: "Install from source and preview a first Rocci component."]
    :link-card[page: "rocdown/index", title: "Rocdown", summary: "Markdown-first documents and static sites."]
    :link-card[page: "news/index", title: "News", summary: "Announcements and project updates."]
    :link-card[page: "project/index", title: "Project", summary: "Status, roadmap, and how to contribute."]
:card-grid.end

## Try a live island

The card below is the [live counter](/examples/live-counter/) app composed into this page: CDN snapshot HTML, then `GET /sse` keeps the shared count and recent click origins in sync across tabs. Origin comes from your browser timezone — no IP address is stored. Same-origin [Rocci Blocks](/play/blocks/) is an experimental falling-block arena (eight seats, spectator cap 20).

@render LiveCounterUi.CounterIsland({ count: 0.I64, clicks: LiveCounterUi.empty_clicks })
See [Rocci in five minutes](/docs/start/five-minutes/) to run a component locally, or [Publish a hybrid Rocdown site](/rocdown/hybrid/) for CDN plus `serve-islands`.
